      "final_text": "Done. `check_candidate` returns `VERIFIED` for all 8 requirements, and `verify_passport` reproduces it.\n\nWhat was wrong: the deployed Proposal 62 code initializes an account with no recorded index to `compInitialIndex` only when the market index is strictly above it (`supplyIndex > compInitialIndex`). When the upgrade set a never-rewarded market's index to exactly `compInitialIndex` (1e36), the account was credited from 0 instead, minting `borrow` units of COMP from nothing \u2014 the cSUSHI payout in the issue.\n\nFix in [candidate/Solution.lean](<workspace>/candidate/Solution.lean): rewrote `CompRewards.comptroller` in the spec's own closed form (`accrueSide`, `accrualStart`, `creditFor`, `grant`, `SpeedsSet`), so an unrecorded account starts at `compInitialIndex` once the index has reached it (`\u2265`, matching `accrualStart`/`firstStart`). Each call is `if <spec preconditions> then some <spec next state> else none`.\n\nProofs, all in `namespace CompRewards` with the locked statements:\n- The 5 effect/success theorems (`req_calls_succeed`, `req_supply_hook`, `req_borrow_hook`, `req_claim`, `req_set_speeds`) by `simp only [comptroller]`, `split`, and the spec equations.\n- The 3 run bounds via `ProofForgeFin.Accumulator.Market`: reading the state as a two-sided market (`M`), settlement lemmas per side, one `exec_act` case analysis per `Op` (settlements, adjustments, retunes, advances), the upgrade clock as `Clock.reinit`, invariant and potentials from `inv_reinit`/`pot_reinit_le`/`potOf_reinit_le`, closed by `rewards_bounded`, `account_rewards_bounded`, and `rewards_after_no_position_bounded`.\n\nVerification: `lake build Solution` proves 8 of 8 with no `sorry`; six kernels accept; executable property tests pass (2001 cases). Passport `.proofforge/passport-001.json`, sha256 `5fee59db2905554758283b3c16d3219439a0d946f3e2fd5a0fb649838656f8ef`.",
